	)
	(text "64 kbit (the HAT+ specification sets no size; the M24C64 is a JLCPCB preferred part, the M24C32 is not).\nAddress 0x51 (A0 high, Stackable class) as shipped; cut jumper 1-2 and bridge 2-3 for 0x50 (Standard class) when the Pi bus\njumpers are closed.  Write protect pulled up with 1k (whole array protected); short the WP test point to the GND pad beside it to program it.\nID_SD / ID_SC carry nothing but the EEPROM and their 3.9k pull-ups (HAT+ specification)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 181.432 35.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "1a5c1d38-f7a3-5830-a1a7-73838e5bcc40")
	)
	(text "Optional Pi bus to the FPGA: solder jumpers, open as shipped, and 1k series resistors"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 105.07 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "2bf3ad0e-0777-5ecc-a852-8c76288b0d9e")
	)
	(text "HAT+ ID EEPROM: 24Cxx, 16-bit addressing, 3.3 V from the Pi"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 181.432 25.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "533dd67c-b8e4-5f27-98ec-63c133aab77c")
	)
	(text "40-pin stacking header, 16 mm board-to-board"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 25.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "78e41462-8142-5fd4-9229-66bbdea36e78")
	)
	(text "Mounting holes: M2.5 on the Pi's hole pattern, tied to GND"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 277.3066 105.07 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a1d77e8b-e794-592c-b9d0-41daf7867a59")
	)
	(text "Power (5 V on pins 2 / 4, 3.3 V on 1 / 17), ground, ID_SD / ID_SC and the nine optional bus lines are used here; every other\npin passes through to the top unconnected (Stackable class).  Footprint: the Pi's own header pattern, seen from above.\nPart: 13.5 mm body on the underside (on the Pi's 2.5 mm header base: 16 mm), 9.8 mm tails through the board (SparkFun PRT-16764,\nmade by 4UCON); not stocked at LCSC, so it is bought in and supplied for assembly."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 35.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a2e2f352-3956-579e-85cf-6b26c60c092b")
	)
	(text "Fiducials: three marks for the assembler's camera, top side"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 414.7066 105.07 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "bbc6f2f2-78d8-561a-8b17-28130dec70c8")
	)
	(text "8  Raspberry Pi HAT+: 40-pin stacking header, ID EEPROM, optional Pi bus jumpers, mounting holes, fiducials"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 14 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3 3)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "d2a17922-184e-5bab-8962-5274f247fcbd")
	)
	(text "I2C1, SPI0 and the UART (nine lines) reach FPGA bank 0 (3.3 V).  The FPGA keeps them as inputs without pulls, also during\nconfiguration (HSWAPEN high), unless the host enables an output; the 1k limits the current if both sides drive."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 110.87 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ee43fd72-1345-53bd-ab3d-35317b9820c3")
	)
